@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title CMA-ES — Derandomized Self-Adaptation for Black-Box Objectives
' Paper: Completely Derandomized Self-Adaptation in Evolution Strategies
' URL:   https://doi.org/10.1162/106365601750190398
' Level: 1

database  "Distribution over θ\nmean m, covariance C" as DIST <<db>>
component "Sample a population\nλ candidate vectors" as POP <<async>>
cloud     "Evaluate fitness\nnoisy, no derivative" as FIT <<cloud>>
component "Select the best μ\nrank only, values discarded" as SEL <<app>>
component "Adapt m and C\nfrom the successful steps" as ADAPT <<host>>

DIST ARROW_QUEUE POP : draw λ samples
POP ARROW_CLOUD FIT : run the simulation / match
FIT ARROW_MAIN SEL : ranking is enough
SEL ARROW_MAIN ADAPT : which directions worked
ADAPT ARROW_MAIN DIST : shift mean, reshape covariance

note bottom of ADAPT
  **Rank-based, so the objective may be anything.**
  CMA-ES needs only an ordering of candidates — no
  gradient, no continuity, not even a stable scale.
  A win rate over played matches qualifies.
  ----
  The covariance matrix is the point: it **learns
  which directions in parameter space matter** and
  how they correlate, so it handles ill-conditioned
  and rotated objectives that coordinate-wise
  hill-climbing stalls on. "Derandomized" refers to
  adapting step size from the actual successful
  steps rather than from separately mutated
  strategy parameters.
  ----
  Requires a fitness signal with real confidence
  bounds, or it optimizes noise — see
  ""../rating-systems/paired-comparison-rating.puml"".
end note
@enduml
